# Copy to .env and configure locally; never commit real credentials.
APP_ENV=development
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=4320
MAIN_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:4320
GAME_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.2:4321
LOCAL_GAMES=1
DATABASE_TLS=disable
SUBMISSIONS_ROOT=data/submissions
EXPORTS_ROOT=data/exports
CLAMD_PORT=3310
# DATABASE_URL and SESSION_SECRET are generated by npm run local:init.

# Production local private storage (illustrative only; values are supplied by the operator,
# never committed). Both public origins must be HTTPS and different registrable domains.
# APP_ENV=production
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# MAIN_ORIGIN=<operator-supplied HTTPS origin>
# GAME_ORIGIN=<operator-supplied second HTTPS origin>
# LOCAL_GAMES=0
# GAME_LISTEN_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.2:4321
# Production opens both listeners only after database, private storage and scanner checks pass.
# The local/public Windows launcher remains development mode; see docs/production-runtime.md.
# DATABASE_URL=<operator-supplied production database URL>
# DATABASE_TLS=verify-full
# SESSION_SECRET=<operator-supplied secret of at least 32 bytes>
# PRIVATE_STORAGE_DRIVER=local
# PRIVATE_STORAGE_ROOT=data/submissions
# PRIVATE_STORAGE_TRUST_ROOT=<optional trusted boundary, e.g. D:\\agp-data when the root is D:\\agp-data\\prod-storage>
# PRIVATE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT=<dedicated Windows service account, e.g. HOST\\svc-agp-main>
# PRIVATE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_SID=<its SID, e.g. S-1-5-21-...; preferred to avoid localised names>
# PRIVATE_STORAGE_EXTRA_SIDS=<optional comma-separated trusted SIDs, e.g. a read-only backup account>
# OBJECT_STORAGE_ENDPOINT / OBJECT_STORAGE_BUCKET must NOT be set in local driver mode.
# The private root must not be frontend/, backend/, data/postgres/ or data/backups/.
# The root, every parent up to the trust boundary (or to the volume root when no
# boundary is set), and the boundary itself must have inheritance disabled and
# only the service account, SYSTEM and Administrators in the ACL. Authenticated
# Users, Users, Everyone, unresolvable principals, untrusted owners and any Deny
# ACE that would strip the service account's required rights cause a fail-closed
# refusal. The service process must run as PRIVATE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT.
# PRIVATE_STORAGE_TRUST_ROOT stops the guard chain at a hardened directory so the
# volume root does not need to be modified: it must be an ancestor of the root,
# never a drive root, and it is still fully validated itself. Actors above the
# boundary can at most delete or rename the whole store (availability); they can
# never inject or read content. See docs/windows-acl-acceptance-plan-2026-11-03.md.
